Hi,

the below is an experimental patch to reduce slighly the power
consumption of AC97 codecs at idle time.  The DAC/ADC are turned
on/off automatically on demand.  With my laptop, it extended about 5
minutes of battery run time.  It's not a big gain, but a few minutes
may become critical in some situation ;)

If you have a laptop with intel8x0, via82xx or atiixp, please give it
a try.  (In theory, it may work with other drivers using ac97, too.)
After applying the patch and reloading the driver, set

	# echo 1 > /proc/asound/card0/codec97#0/ac97#0-0+power

The proc file name might be different depending on the codec id.

The drawback of this patch is that it may produce a pop noise at
opening a sound device onsome machines.


Takashi


